<title>PORTUGAL: Second Neves Corvo copper ballot rejects offer.</title>
<headline>Second Neves Corvo copper ballot rejects offer.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A management offer of improved conditions in exchange for Sunday working has been rejected by a second and final ballot of miners at the Neves Corvo copper facility in southern Portugal.</p>
<p>The rejection by members of the night shift had been expected after the morning and afternoon shifts had spurned the terms earlier on Thursday.</p>
<p>Somincor, the state-controlled company that operates the 107,000 tonnes per year mine, had offered more holidays in return for miners accepting Sunday shifts. But union leaders said the managament needed to improve the offer.</p>
</text>
